WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.180
How can we live free?

00:00:02.180 --> 00:00:04.340
Government imposes so many rules,

00:00:04.340 --> 00:00:06.460
many of which we don’t agree with.

00:00:06.460 --> 00:00:08.620
So, what could we do?

00:00:08.620 --> 00:00:10.980
Not happy with the way government runs?

00:00:10.990 --> 00:00:12.820
How about starting your own country?

00:00:12.820 --> 00:00:14.660
Build a city in the ocean.

00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:16.260
[Music]

00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:18.289
It’s called Seasteading.

00:00:18.289 --> 00:00:19.940
The idea is that if people move

00:00:19.940 --> 00:00:21.900
at least 12 miles off-shore,

00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:24.960
they can build their own cities, or country,

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:28.899
and live free from government’s suffocating rules.

00:00:28.899 --> 00:00:33.090
Unfortunately, nothing like this has been built yet.

00:00:33.090 --> 00:00:34.300
This is just an animation,

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:37.030
showing what seasteads might look like in the future.

00:00:37.030 --> 00:00:38.610
To the first seastead.

00:00:38.610 --> 00:00:42.000
But this year, Chad and Nadia Elwartowski set up this

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:46.100
small Seastead 13 miles of the coast of Thailand.

00:00:51.740 --> 00:00:53.940
As long as people can create these seasteads

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:57.850
voluntarily and people can quit them voluntarily,

00:00:57.850 --> 00:00:58.780
then you'll have a market

00:00:58.780 --> 00:01:00.829
of competing governance providers.

00:01:00.829 --> 00:01:03.040
Joe Quirk runs The Seasteading Institute,

00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:05.479
which promotes the floating islands.

00:01:05.479 --> 00:01:07.900
We need a new place to experiment with new

00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:10.660
rules appropriate for modern technologies.

00:01:10.660 --> 00:01:12.040
What a great idea!

00:01:12.040 --> 00:01:14.720
Unfortunately, that first seastead

00:01:14.720 --> 00:01:16.900
recently came to a bad end.

00:01:16.900 --> 00:01:18.140
More on that shortly.

00:01:18.140 --> 00:01:21.200
But first, let’s hear more about the idea.

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:23.580
Innovators innovating in the 21st century

00:01:23.580 --> 00:01:26.799
are being held back by rules written in the 1970s.

00:01:26.800 --> 00:01:29.020
But we need some rules.

00:01:29.020 --> 00:01:31.280
Seasteaders don't have a problem

00:01:31.280 --> 00:01:34.200
with regulations per se.

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:36.740
Humans need rules to interact.

00:01:36.740 --> 00:01:39.480
We have a problem with the monopoly over the

00:01:39.480 --> 00:01:42.240
provision and enforcement of regulations.

00:01:42.249 --> 00:01:45.140
Liberate humanity from politicians.

00:01:45.140 --> 00:01:48.479
Yes, we don't need politicians.

00:01:48.479 --> 00:01:50.700
They're not smart enough to make decisions for us.

00:01:50.700 --> 00:01:52.220
Without American rules,

00:01:52.220 --> 00:01:57.250
some will be shooting up heroin or abusing children.

00:01:57.250 --> 00:01:58.859
We have that in our country right now.

00:01:58.859 --> 00:02:01.040
But if I move 12 miles off shore,

00:02:01.040 --> 00:02:03.819
I'm going to be so incentivized to set a better example.

00:02:03.819 --> 00:02:05.859
Because the world's eyes are going to be on me.

00:02:05.859 --> 00:02:08.470
I got to convince investors to invest in it.

00:02:08.470 --> 00:02:10.300
I got to convince people to move there.

00:02:10.300 --> 00:02:12.920
I got to convince people to take jobs there.

00:02:12.920 --> 00:02:14.180
I think in such an environment,

00:02:14.180 --> 00:02:16.200
it's going to be much more difficult to create

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:19.040
evil islands of heroin shooting

00:02:19.040 --> 00:02:21.620
than it is to create positive innovations

00:02:21.620 --> 00:02:22.860
that improve people's lives.

00:02:22.860 --> 00:02:26.690
We are Carnival believe fun is a choice.

00:02:26.690 --> 00:02:29.260
He says the world already has a form of seasteads—

00:02:29.260 --> 00:02:30.770
the cruise ship.

00:02:30.770 --> 00:02:32.760
Most cruise ships fly the flag of say,

00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:35.860
Panama or Liberia, and they're sort of

00:02:35.860 --> 00:02:38.670
de facto self-governing.

00:02:38.670 --> 00:02:42.260
Liberia has no capacity to enforce rules

00:02:42.260 --> 00:02:45.830
on the three and a half thousand ships that fly its flag.

00:02:45.830 --> 00:02:48.860
So a captain is a de facto dictator.

00:02:48.860 --> 00:02:50.020
Why doesn't he become a tyrant?

00:02:50.020 --> 00:02:51.360
And the answer is because

00:02:51.360 --> 00:02:53.500
people can choose another cruise line.

00:02:53.500 --> 00:02:56.120
The Seasteading Institute approaches politicians,

00:02:56.120 --> 00:02:58.120
saying "We'll bring our own land,

00:02:58.120 --> 00:03:00.520
we'll float just off shore.

00:03:00.520 --> 00:03:02.940
And if it succeeds, we share in the prosperity,

00:03:02.940 --> 00:03:05.400
if it fails, we absorb the cost."

00:03:05.400 --> 00:03:08.320
Minds can be opened to a little bit more freedom,

00:03:08.320 --> 00:03:09.720
a little further out to shore.

00:03:09.720 --> 00:03:11.480
[Car sound]

00:03:11.480 --> 00:03:14.340
Minds were opened in China when tiny Hong Kong

00:03:14.340 --> 00:03:18.020
showed that having fewer rules could bring prosperity.

00:03:18.020 --> 00:03:19.260
China very rapidly,

00:03:19.260 --> 00:03:21.740
because of the example set by Hong Kong,

00:03:21.740 --> 00:03:24.760
started creating these special economic zones.

00:03:24.760 --> 00:03:27.520
Special economic zones are similar to Seasteads.

00:03:27.520 --> 00:03:29.060
They have fewer rules.

00:03:29.060 --> 00:03:31.160
At least a half billion Chinese people

00:03:31.160 --> 00:03:32.840
have exited extreme poverty

00:03:32.840 --> 00:03:35.350
by moving to these new jurisdictions.

00:03:35.350 --> 00:03:36.940
So why don't the Chinese leaders

00:03:36.940 --> 00:03:39.680
or any political leaders say,

00:03:39.680 --> 00:03:42.540
"This works, we'll do it for the whole country."

00:03:42.540 --> 00:03:43.660
Never for the whole country.

00:03:43.660 --> 00:03:46.350
Why not? I would.

00:03:46.350 --> 00:03:47.350
I would too.

00:03:47.350 --> 00:03:49.830
But that's why you and I don't have political power.

00:03:49.830 --> 00:03:52.420
Unfortunately, in China,

00:03:52.420 --> 00:03:55.400
those with political power didn’t want to give it up.

00:03:55.400 --> 00:03:58.820
They did not expand freedom to the whole country.

00:03:58.820 --> 00:04:00.020
So something like Seasteading

00:04:00.020 --> 00:04:02.390
would be an important experiment.

00:04:02.390 --> 00:04:04.500
Chad and Nadia hoped their Seastead

00:04:04.500 --> 00:04:06.040
would be the first of many.

00:04:07.850 --> 00:04:09.480
They thought they would do a demonstration

00:04:09.480 --> 00:04:13.020
project of this tiny cabin and demonstrate

00:04:13.020 --> 00:04:14.800
the world that they can make it cheap.

00:04:14.800 --> 00:04:16.510
And they thought nobody would care.

00:04:16.510 --> 00:04:17.860
To everyone's surprise

00:04:17.860 --> 00:04:20.739
the Thai navy took exception to this.

00:04:20.739 --> 00:04:21.960
Two aspiring seasteaders

00:04:21.960 --> 00:04:24.760
have had their property raided by the Thai navy.

00:04:24.760 --> 00:04:28.210
Chad and Nadia left their island shortly before the raid.

00:04:28.210 --> 00:04:30.660
They got nervous when they saw

00:04:30.660 --> 00:04:32.900
a reconnaissance plane flying overhead

00:04:32.900 --> 00:04:34.780
Now they are on the run.

00:04:34.780 --> 00:04:36.500
… could, in theory, face the death penalty

00:04:36.500 --> 00:04:38.889
for violating Thai sovereignty.

00:04:38.889 --> 00:04:40.980
That would be quite a price

00:04:40.980 --> 00:04:44.300
for trying to live on the high seas.

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:47.100
It's irresponsible not to improve society

00:04:47.100 --> 00:04:49.390
by setting better examples.

00:04:49.390 --> 00:04:51.140
And I think people with the best ideas

00:04:51.140 --> 00:04:53.860
should be given an opportunity to do that voluntarily

00:04:53.860 --> 00:04:55.880
and pay the consequences of their failures

00:04:55.880 --> 00:04:58.080
and get the profits if they succeed.

00:04:58.080 --> 00:05:00.620
Good for Chad and Nadia for trying.

